From: Wine Fox
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Menus of tray icons where the tray was clicked (wlr-layer-shell).

A tray icon's menu has no shown window of ours to be an xdg_popup of. Its window is often hidden
in the tray: Wine's menus were then subsurfaces of that hidden window and not shown at all, and
Qt's (Battle.net) were windows in the middle of the screen. When the window is shown, the menu
was placed from where Wine has that window, not where the compositor shows it, nor at the icon.

Such menus and popups are layer surfaces now (zwlr_layer_shell_v1, KWin, wlroots compositors),
on the overlay layer, where Wine has them on the output: the menus Wine's xdg_popups are, and
Qt's (QWindowPopup classes), when their owner is hidden, a layer surface (a submenu) or none, or
when they open at the cursor while the pointer is on no window of ours. Unreal Engine's windows
are left as they are. Another application taking the keyboard closes them, as a click out of
them, which they do not see, would. wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1.xml has the interfaces of
wlroots' protocol. Without the protocol (GNOME) nothing changes.

